   "fix": "Add `@[grind =]` to `twist_zero`, `twist_singleton`, the eight `LightConeField.twist_*` value lemmas, and the `quarkNumber_zero/_cons/_singleton/_add` and `quarkNumber_quark/_quarkBar/_fieldStrength` lemmas, so `grind` can evaluate a concrete field content and its quark number; alternatively drop the four `grind` attributes rather than ship a set that closes nothing.",
   "issue": "`twist_cons` (290) and `twist_add` (323) carry `@[grind =]`, and `one_le_twist` (220) / `card_le_twist` (341) carry `@[grind .]` \u2014 these four are the only `grind` attributes in the repository \u2014 but the lemmas they reduce to carry only `@[simp]`: `twist_zero` (278), `twist_singleton` (306) and the eight per-field values `twist_quark_good` \u2026 `twist_fieldStrength_minusTransverse` (187\u2013204). `grind` normalizes with its own `grind_norm` set, not the default `simp` set, so after E-matching `twist_cons` on `twist {quarkBar .good, quark .good}` it has no fact for `(quark .good).twist` or `twist 0` and stalls. The same gap covers the `quarkNumber` family (206\u2013212, 280, 294, 309, 327), which is what the `quarkNumber O = 0` hypothesis of `twist_eq_two_iff_of_quarkNumber_eq_zero` (433) and `twist_eq_three_iff_of_quarkNumber_eq_zero` (450) rests on.",
   "line": "290"
  }
